# Shell and Utilities (POSIX.2) options. The utilities are not part of this module: a provider
# of a complete, conforming utility set for an option (a multi-call binary module such as toybox)
# selects the matching symbol, and <unistd.h> and sysconf() then report the option. A provider
# that lacks any utility of a set does not select it: the options are all-or-nothing.

config POSIX2_SHELL_UTILITIES
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the Shell and Utilities volume's mandatory utilities, sh included;
	  _POSIX2_VERSION is reported.

config POSIX2_C_DEV
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the C-Language Development Utilities (c99, lex, yacc); _POSIX2_C_DEV
	  is reported.

config POSIX2_CHAR_TERM
	bool
	help
	  At least one terminal type supports every operation of the Terminal Characteristics
	  option; _POSIX2_CHAR_TERM is reported.

config POSIX2_FORT_DEV
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the FORTRAN Development Utilities (fort77); _POSIX2_FORT_DEV is
	  reported.

config POSIX2_FORT_RUN
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the FORTRAN Runtime Utilities (asa); _POSIX2_FORT_RUN is reported.

config POSIX2_LOCALEDEF
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the localedef utility and supports the creation of locales;
	  _POSIX2_LOCALEDEF is reported.

config POSIX2_SW_DEV
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the Software Development Utilities (ar, make, nm, strip);
	  _POSIX2_SW_DEV is reported.

config POSIX2_UPE
	bool
	help
	  The image carries the User Portability Utilities (alias, at, batch, bg, crontab, csplit,
	  ctags, df, du, ex, expand, fc, fg, file, jobs, man, mesg, more, newgrp, nice, nohup,
	  patch, ps, renice, split, strings, tabs, talk, time, tput, unalias, unexpand, uudecode,
	  uuencode, vi, who, write); _POSIX2_UPE is reported.
